# Public entry point. Caddy terminates TLS (auto Let's Encrypt) and
# reverse-proxies to the web container over the internal Docker network.
# The browser only ever talks to `web`'s origin; web itself rewrites
# /api/* to the api container (see web/next.config.mjs), so nothing else
# needs to be exposed.
#
# Three hostnames on purpose:
#   - shbexpertai.online / www — the real domain (Hostinger DNS, A record
#     -> the Elastic IP). This is what demos and users should use.
#   - app.<eip-dashed>.sslip.io — fallback that needs no DNS at all, since
#     sslip.io resolves the IP embedded in the name. Keeps the site
#     reachable if the domain's DNS is ever misconfigured or expires.
#
# Caddy manages each hostname's certificate independently, so a hostname
# whose DNS is broken cannot take down the ones that work. Certificates
# live in the `caddy_data` volume and survive redeploys — a rebuild does
# NOT re-issue them, so there is no Let's Encrypt rate-limit risk here.
shbexpertai.online, www.shbexpertai.online, app.45-57-135-39.sslip.io {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy web:3000
}
